      <div type="clause" n="24.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 24.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.12"/> he gewitnesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.17"/> hæbbe, swa we<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.18"/> her<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.19"/> beforan cwædon, þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.20"/> tyme hit man þriwa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.21"/>; æt þam feorðan cyrre agnige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.22"/> hit oððe agyfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.14"/> þam þe hit age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf he witnysse habbe, swa we ær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.7"/> cwǽdon, ðonne tyma<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.8"/> hit man ðriwa; æt ðam feorðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.8"/> cyrre áhnige hit oððe agyfe ðam ðe hit age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif he gewittnysse hæbbe, swa hær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.1"/> beforan cwædon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.1"/> is, þon tyme hit man ðrywa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.3"/>; æt þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> feorðan cerre agnie hit oððe agyfe þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe hit age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Si testimonium habeat, sicut prediximus, tunc liceat inde ter aduocari; et quarta uice proprietur aut reddatur ei cuius erit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi tales testes habuerit, quales supra diximus, warantem uocet; et ille uocatus uocet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.15"/> alium, si potest, et tertius adhuc tertium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.star-2"/> uocet, si potest; et tertius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.star2"/> suum faciet, si ualet; quodsi non ualet, reddatur ei, qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/> iuste habere debet.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Si uero testimonium, sicut prediximus, habuit, ter fiat attestacio; tertio autem uendicet aut reddat illi cuius illud est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="24.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="186" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf he witnysse<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_24-2.robnote.fn.6"/> habbe, swa we ær cwædon<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_24-2.robnote.fn.7"/>, ðonne tyma hit man ðriwa; æt þam feorðam cyrre áhnige hit oððe agyfe ðam ðe hit age.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="266" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf he gewitnesse hæbbe, swa we her beforan cwædon, þonne tyme hit man þriwa; æt þam feorðan cyrre, agnige hit oððe agyfe þam þe hit age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Jedoch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.de.1"/> wenn der [verklagte Besitzer Erwerbs-]Zeugenschaft hat, wie wir hier zuvor (früher <hi rend="italic">B</hi>?) verordnet haben, dann kann es [das Angeschlagene] dreimal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.de.2"/> einem Gewährsmanne zugeschoben werden; beim vierten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_24-2.lnote.de.3"/> Male [aber] muss er [der Bezogene] es als sein Eigen erweisen oder dem, welchem es gehört, zurückgeben.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if he [the accused possessor] has witness [of acquisition], as we have laid down here above (before, B?), then it [the attached item] may be vouched to warranty three times; the fourth time [the person vouched] must prove it his own or give it back to the one to whom it belongs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="187" ed="#robertson"/>And if he has witnesses in accordance with what we have declared above, vouching to warranty shall take place three times. On the fourth occasion he shall prove his claim<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-2.robnote.n.1"/> to it or give it back to its rightful owner.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And if he has witness, as we have said above, one may vouch to warranty three times; on the fourth occasion he is either to make good his claim to it or give it back to the owner.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="267" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if he has witnesses, just as we have set forth here, then he is to vouch to warranty three times; on the fourth time, he shall prove his ownership or return it to its proper owner.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="327"><ref target="clause:IICn_24">II Cn 24</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*24</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_45-2">Leis Wl 45.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 327, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">we: omitted A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">her beforan: ær B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">cwædon: cwædon is A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quarto <hi rend="italic">zu bessern</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quarto to be corrected</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">für</hi> hær?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for hær?</seg></note>
